{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552033-dtf-the-fallen-have-a-hierarchy-too","id":1552033,"title":"DtF: The fallen have a hierarchy too?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-03T09:16:13-07:00","id":1552033,"title":"DtF: The fallen have a hierarchy too?","content":"The fallen angels in &quot;Demon the Fallen&quot; have their hierarchy too?<br /> <br /> If yes, someone can explain me how it's structured?<br /> <br /> I failed to find informations on the web. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T09:34:19-07:00","id":1552034,"title":"","content":"Demon ranks are as Such:<br /> Lucifer Himself<br /> Archdukes<br /> Dukes<br /> Barons<br /> Overlords<br /> Lords<br /> Fell Knights<br /> Lesser Angels/Demons(the rank of player characters)<br /> <br /> Rank is determined by how powerful a demon is, measured in how high their willpower, permanent faith, and number of dots in lores. A player character can qualify as a &quot;Fell Knight&quot; if they achieve Willpower 8, Permanent Faith 3, and 6 dots in lores. On the other end, becoming a Duke would require willpower 10, permanent faith of 6+, and 48 dots in lores.<br /> Within these ranks there's also a measure of soft power/social influence that can make demons of the same rank more important than others. This is measured by the Eminence background. An Eminence 3 fell knight is &quot;higher rank&quot; than an Eminence 2 fell knight, but both are lower rank than an Eminence 2 lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T10:50:50-07:00","id":1552035,"title":"","content":"Thank you this is useful.<br /> <br /> They also have a structured society like cainites (winth the equivalent of a Prince and so on) or they're lone wolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T11:18:45-07:00","id":1552038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552033-dtf-the-fallen-have-a-hierarchy-too?p=1552035#post1552035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you this is useful.<br /> <br /> They also have a structured society like cainites (winth the equivalent of a Prince and so on) or they're lone wolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Most demons are pretty fresh from escaping hell and barely even understand their own memories from the war of wrath, let alone navigate the modern world. There are pockets with fully established demonic courts and organized factions, for example Los Angelos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T12:52:59-07:00","id":1552040,"title":"","content":"<b>City of Angels</b> go deep in this<br /> The <b>Infernal Court</b> is the heart of the Fallen society - the remanant from the War, a system Lucifer hismelf designed and created<br /> <br /> <b>Tyrants</b> are the masters of Infernal Courts, the ultimate authorities (tho' they are still kept on a leash by their True Names by their superiors who are still in the Abyss and too &quot;big&quot; to fit thought the craks and escape. Most of them were Dukes during the Wars, but after the Escape lesser Demons managed to snach the tittle by political machinations, clever maneuvers, ruthlessness and social manipulations - aka. your avarage Cainite Prince in a nuttshell<br /> The Tyranst are aided/ruls with the <b>Pentarchy</b> aka the <b>Five Ministries</b><br /> <b>Ministry of Eagles</b>, the Watchers - charged with gaining intelligence, information of any kind, be it mundane information about the mortal infrastructure and political landscape, lost lore from the ages before their imprisonment or supernatural activity that could threaten the Court. They are teachers, archivists and spies. Their leader is the <i>Most Vigilant Watcher.</i><br /> <b>Ministry of Aurochs</b>, the Warders - charged with the defense of the Court and enforce it's laws, they act as judges in the case that the laws they protect are broken. Their leader is the <i>Lord Harrier</i>\u200b<br /> <b>Ministry of Lions</b>, the Swords - charged with with fighting against threats to the Court. They are elite soldiers. While the Ministry of Aurochs focuses on deffense, the Ministry of Lions focus on the offense. Their leader is the <i>Lord-General</i>\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Ministry of Dragons</b>, the Censors - charged with the inter-Court affairs, their task is questioning and challenging authority and watch signs of corruption and betrayal. They are empowered to investigate everyone within the Courts and weed out the incompetent Demons who are not clever enough to avoid them. Their leader is the <i>Lord Inquisitor</i>\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Ministry of Dust</b>, (or the Ministry of Man) the Guides - charge with the safekeeping of the mortal flock as well as the advancement of the Court. They manages mortal media and institutions, keeping them away from Court infrastructure as well as increasing the general amount of Faith within the population; they are who tend and cares about the Humans (realitve, of course. Faith is tricky and the Ministry could support religious institutions to boost it... or run the city down so that people cling even more tightly to their beliefs and cling in faith. Or be more willing to &quot;sel ltheir souls&quot;) Their leadier is the <i>Speaker of the Fallen Tower</i> or the <i>Guide of the Blind</i>.<br /> <br /> On one hand the Court system is the remnant of a bygone era and the Human-host and the new World introduced several problems, like financial supervision - something the Sebattu never really needed during the War but now it is very focal - for example or the fact they cant roam around in their ture form and throw around powers, they have to be clever when it comes to inner-court conflicts or external threats.<br /> <br /> To complicate the matter - as if the whole House and Choir wouldn't be enough - the Court members more often than not face some conflict of interest<br /> Every Sebettu have a Bigger Fish behind them who ordered them to do everything to help them escape - in some cases an Earthbound are theri master. Among many things that is an either concious or suboncious driving goal behind their every moves, becasue they were Commanded by their True Name to help their masters to escape from the Abyss and not all of them happy about this, especially because those Bigger Fish are not really friends and ideally would let their compatition rot in the Abyss.<br /> This of course forces them to dance a very complicate dance in the Court<br /> So, House, Choir, Court, Infernal Master... and then on the top of it, the Factions.<br /> Sooner or later you have to land in a Faction<br /> <b>Cryptics</b> - seek information on the nature of existence for a variety of purposes<br /> <b>Faustians</b> - believe strongly in the abilities and talents of humans... and how to use/exploit them for their own goals<br /> <b>Luciferans - &quot;</b>Lucifer's Army&quot; , find and restore Lucifer to power. They are an Army that have a hard time figuring out who they are supposed to fight. No Elohim around so they fight the Earthbound. The other Factions. The Humans. They lack a clear enemy but in turn wuite militant; divided into three <i>Legions</i>, the <b>Legion of Majestic Liberation</b> serves as the investigators of the Luciferans\u200b, <b>Legion of Glorius Victory</b> is the actual army of the Luciferans\u200b and <b>Legion of Stark Defiance</b>\u200b, it members serve as the bureaucrats that keeps the entire Faction running.\u200b<br /> <b>Raveners</b> - nihilists and cynics who revel in the destruction of everything in Creation either to lure out God and the Elohim to fight them or destroy them once and for all and end the suffering. But contrary of popular belief they are not mindless killing machines, most are actually quite intelligent and cunning <br /> <b>Reconcilers</b>\u200b\u200b - they believe they chose the wrong path in rebelling against God and wish to make amends in some way. They hope they will be forgiven for their transgressions and be welcomed back into His arms. Or at least they want a return to the way things were before The Fall. <br /> <br /> In a Court the Ministry-membership and the Faction-membership easly could clash in the looming shadow of the aforementioned Bigger Fish (and/or if you realyl want to complicate life, a lingering few Earthbound too that started to revive its Cult in the City and srpeading...) with a healthy dose of Human influence thanks to the host body's memories. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T19:56:49-07:00","id":1552048,"title":"","content":"Basically it's both more complex and simpler than Cainites.<br /> <br /> On one hand, between remnant structures of the War, Factions, True Name Blackmail (which may or may not be the case for any given Fallen) and the new structures, everything made for a population that potentially numbers in the millions, even billions (even if most are in Hell), Demons have an actual complex society.<br /> <br /> Yet, on the other hand the current form of this society is effectively new. The structures from the time of the War are destroyed, even if some are attached to them, the Factions are brand new and mostly informal, without real authority over their members, and the new structures, the Courts as they exist now, are even newer and varied from place to place.<br /> <br /> Los Angeles is a very complex example, but it's also the biggest and most developed Court, it is literally an outlier and not the standard for everywhere else. Outside it, a lot depends on personal relationships between the Fallen as they meet each other, and how many of them are in a given place (which can be anything from thousands to just a couple). So they have a lot of reference on how to structure their society, but in practice most of it is free-form on most places, more than the delicate power balances among Vampires.<br /> <br /> Even because Demons don't compete for resources the same way Vampires do. Faith is far easier to acquire in the long run than Blood and deplete slower, so any given human population can potentially support a far bigger Demon population than they'll ever have really to. This takes out a lot of the pressure vampiric society has on its structure just for basic function. Demons are moved mostly by their long term goals, beliefs and interests than by the alien needs of the undead. Which kind of means you're just as much a part of their hidden society as you want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}